WEBVTT

00:02.028 --> 00:03.530
<i>Previously on</i> Lost:

00:03.571 --> 00:06.491
You gotta trust me.
I am trying to help you.

00:06.533 --> 00:09.577
- Do I know you?
- I'm George Minkowski.

00:09.619 --> 00:12.664
- Communications officer.
- Where is the radio room?

00:12.705 --> 00:14.864
I'll take you there.

00:14.916 --> 00:17.408
How do we get out of here?

00:17.460 --> 00:19.952
Through the door.

00:20.004 --> 00:22.882
Looks like you guys
have a friend on this boat.

00:24.175 --> 00:25.802
You're pregnant?

00:27.262 --> 00:31.047
Juliet. She was their fertility doctor
studying pregnant women.

00:31.099 --> 00:35.270
The reason the Others wanted her baby
was for research.

00:35.311 --> 00:39.399
- What happens to pregnant women?
- They die.

00:39.441 --> 00:42.610
You want me to help you and your baby.
I have answers.

00:42.652 --> 00:46.489
- But you have to come with me now.
- The baby isn't Jin's.

00:48.450 --> 00:52.620
I'm gonna determine the date of
conception. If you got pregnant here...

00:54.164 --> 00:56.207
We'll cross that bridge
when we come to it.

00:56.249 --> 01:00.879
The baby was conceived eight weeks ago.
You got pregnant on the island.

01:00.920 --> 01:03.465
So how long do I have?

01:05.216 --> 01:09.262
Most of the women made it into
the middle of their second trimester.

01:09.304 --> 01:11.306
Nobody made it to their third.

01:27.322 --> 01:28.907
Lapidus!

01:39.042 --> 01:40.585
You ready?

01:41.586 --> 01:42.962
I'll be up.

01:45.340 --> 01:47.300
Don't be late, Frank.

02:00.146 --> 02:03.483
- Regina.
- Frank.

02:03.525 --> 02:07.821
- I didn't hear you.
- Sorry. Didn't mean to spook ya.

02:07.862 --> 02:10.824
The captain wanted me to bring
these guys some grub.

02:10.907 --> 02:12.826
OK.

02:14.244 --> 02:16.329
You know, your book's upside down.

02:24.254 --> 02:25.713
Just trying to help.

02:31.928 --> 02:35.682
Thought I'd check in on you guys,
bring you some food.

02:35.723 --> 02:39.018
- How you feeling, by the way?
- Much better, thanks.

02:39.060 --> 02:43.012
Why are we held captive? We had nothing
to do with Minkowski's death.

02:43.064 --> 02:48.445
Nothing to do with Minkowski. Captain
wasn't happy you busted out of sick bay

02:48.486 --> 02:51.062
- and into our radio room.
- We didn't bust out.

02:51.114 --> 02:53.408
The door was left open.

02:53.450 --> 02:56.984
- And we assumed it was you.
- Why the hell would I do that?

02:58.329 --> 03:00.738
Any contact
with our people on the beach?

03:01.458 --> 03:04.461
No luck. Something
must've happened to their phone.

03:08.131 --> 03:10.456
Lima beans?

03:10.508 --> 03:12.969
Sorry, we had a problem
in the kitchen.

03:13.887 --> 03:15.513
Just stay put, all right?

03:17.390 --> 03:19.392
I still want to talk to the captain.

03:21.019 --> 03:22.479
No, you don't.

03:26.107 --> 03:27.692
Regina.

04:07.482 --> 04:09.317
Let's talk about baby names.

04:10.735 --> 04:12.977
Good. You're getting better.

04:14.072 --> 04:15.156
But no, Jin.

04:54.362 --> 04:55.613
Deal.

08:08.681 --> 08:09.766
What happened?

08:09.808 --> 08:13.728
You mean before or after
the redhead knocked me out?

08:15.188 --> 08:16.470
She hit you?

08:16.523 --> 08:19.734
When I ran into them
on my way back from Locke's camp.

08:19.776 --> 08:21.058
Why would she do that?

08:22.195 --> 08:26.783
Guess she didn't want to explain why she
was on her way to a poison gas factory.

08:28.868 --> 08:31.194
Juliet told Jack it was a power station.

08:31.246 --> 08:34.290
Why would Juliet lie about that?

08:34.332 --> 08:35.583
Force of habit.

08:37.419 --> 08:40.255
- Why were they going there?
- To turn it off.

08:40.296 --> 08:43.748
Deactivate the gas. They wanted
to earn some brownie points.

08:46.511 --> 08:49.806
Do you think they're
really going to rescue us?

08:49.848 --> 08:52.767
In the time they've been here,
they've talked about a lot.

08:52.809 --> 08:56.146
And none involved rescuing us.

09:16.833 --> 09:17.917
Good morning.

09:20.253 --> 09:21.671
Good morning.

09:21.713 --> 09:24.799
I hope they resolve
their kitchen issues.

09:31.639 --> 09:32.755
Sayid.

09:34.976 --> 09:36.478
What's that?

09:42.901 --> 09:44.861
It's a note.

09:46.529 --> 09:50.867
Three days ago,
when I was in Locke's camp,

09:50.909 --> 09:53.369
Ben claimed he had a spy on this boat.

10:13.473 --> 10:16.601
Hello. My name is Sun.

10:16.684 --> 10:19.604
Hi, Sun. Hi. I'm Daniel.

10:23.650 --> 10:25.610
Something I can help you with?

10:26.736 --> 10:28.655
I'm two months pregnant.

10:30.281 --> 10:34.150
Oh, you're... Wow. That's...

10:34.202 --> 10:37.987
- Congratulations.
- So you're here to rescue us?

10:42.502 --> 10:44.712
It's a simple question.

10:44.754 --> 10:47.924
Are you or are you not
going to rescue us?

10:49.843 --> 10:51.594
The thing is...

10:54.264 --> 10:56.474
...it's not really my call, Sun.

10:57.559 --> 10:59.394
Then whose call is it?

11:03.648 --> 11:05.233
Thank you.

11:07.277 --> 11:09.571
Can you pass the cereal?

11:17.537 --> 11:20.457
- Pretty good English, Jin.
- Thank you.

11:20.498 --> 11:24.252
I understand better than I speak.

11:26.045 --> 11:28.715
Sun been teaching you
or you just picking it up?

11:28.757 --> 11:32.343
Sun teach me. Sawyer, too.

11:33.470 --> 11:37.599
- Sun is better.
- I bet.

11:40.477 --> 11:43.396
Hey, Sun. How you feeling?

11:43.438 --> 11:45.899
I'm good, thank you.

11:47.400 --> 11:50.445
The morning sickness has stopped,
which has been nice.

11:51.362 --> 11:52.614
That's good.

11:53.448 --> 11:57.660
Well, if you need anything,
just let me know. OK?

12:03.041 --> 12:05.001
Would you like some breakfast?

12:43.289 --> 12:44.874
What are you doing?

12:47.627 --> 12:51.329
I needed another bottle
of those vitamins you gave me.

12:51.381 --> 12:54.832
- The prenatals.
- You could have just asked.

12:54.884 --> 12:57.345
You're right. I should have.

12:57.387 --> 12:59.712
What happened to the
last ones I gave you?

13:01.349 --> 13:04.018
- Sorry?
- The last bottle I gave you.

13:04.060 --> 13:05.603
There should be 20 left.

13:07.188 --> 13:08.773
Are you planning a trip?

13:10.108 --> 13:12.235
Please, just give me the vitamins.

13:14.112 --> 13:15.864
Where are you going, Sun?

13:18.658 --> 13:21.494
- We're going to Locke's camp.
- What?

13:23.037 --> 13:26.656
- Why?
- Because I don't trust these people.

13:26.708 --> 13:28.866
Whether you trust them, you can't go.

13:28.918 --> 13:33.746
Locke doesn't want to leave the island.
I've told you, pregnant women,

13:33.840 --> 13:35.258
they don't survive here.

13:35.341 --> 13:38.052
Yes, you did tell me that.

13:39.763 --> 13:41.045
You don't believe me?

13:42.766 --> 13:46.467
Look, I know I've
been less than truthful

13:46.519 --> 13:50.982
about certain things since coming here,
but I promise you, Sun, I promise you,

13:51.024 --> 13:53.349
I'm not lying about this.

13:55.361 --> 13:59.657
After everything you've confided in me,
I should at least have your trust.

14:02.619 --> 14:06.154
Claire's baby is fine. I feel fine.

14:06.206 --> 14:10.418
All I have are your stories
that I'm going to get sick.

14:10.460 --> 14:13.838
I'm going to do what's best for me
and for my baby.

14:13.880 --> 14:17.717
Because no, I don't trust you.

15:55.106 --> 15:56.691
Taxi!

17:31.035 --> 17:33.955
Once you hit this stream,
you wanna head northwest.

17:34.080 --> 17:37.208
Pretty much in a straight line
for about a day and a half.

17:37.250 --> 17:40.628
- Thank you.
- I'm gonna have to tell Jack.

17:42.297 --> 17:44.257
I'll give you a long head start.

17:44.340 --> 17:46.885
I'd tell him,
but he wouldn't understand.

17:46.926 --> 17:48.887
No, he wouldn't.

17:51.014 --> 17:53.256
You better get going.

17:54.726 --> 17:56.811
- Be safe, OK?
- Thank you.

17:56.853 --> 17:59.262
She's not going anywhere.

17:59.314 --> 18:03.234
- Sun, this is a bad idea.
- What concern is it of yours?

18:03.276 --> 18:07.572
Do you understand your
wife's medical condition right now?

18:08.698 --> 18:11.743
- Translate for me.
- No.

18:13.536 --> 18:16.456
Your wife is very sick.

18:17.165 --> 18:20.700
If she doesn't get off this island
in three weeks, she will die.

18:27.092 --> 18:32.170
If you let her go,
your wife is in danger, Jin. Danger.

18:33.848 --> 18:36.976
Where Sun go, I go.

18:39.771 --> 18:42.315
Sun. Please.

18:47.779 --> 18:49.322
Jin.

18:50.657 --> 18:52.450
Your wife had an affair.

18:56.663 --> 19:00.364
- What?
- Sun was with another man.

19:04.087 --> 19:06.329
She thought the baby was his.

20:21.623 --> 20:23.708
Hey! You going fishing?

20:25.418 --> 20:27.994
Mind if I tag along?

20:31.174 --> 20:35.011
Oh, I'm sorry.
I didn't mean to interrupt.

20:35.053 --> 20:37.055
No. Come.

20:37.097 --> 20:38.681
You sure?

20:40.767 --> 20:43.394
Yes. Come.

21:06.209 --> 21:09.003
We're the only two married guys
on the island.

21:11.506 --> 21:13.133
Married.

21:14.384 --> 21:18.336
- Married.
- Yeah, well, not to each other, no.

21:18.388 --> 21:20.181
You got it.

21:21.808 --> 21:23.966
It's not easy, is it?

21:24.018 --> 21:27.803
I mean, it's wonderful,
but let's face it.

21:27.856 --> 21:31.234
Every decision that you make
takes twice as long.

21:31.276 --> 21:33.486
You always gotta talk them into it.

21:38.908 --> 21:42.495
Rose... has cancer.

21:45.582 --> 21:49.085
She's sick. Dying.

21:51.087 --> 21:53.965
Well, she was dying.

21:54.048 --> 21:56.050
She says she's better now.

21:57.093 --> 22:01.139
She says it's this place. The island.

22:03.475 --> 22:08.302
But when the camp split up,
I was sure she'd want to go with Locke.

22:09.647 --> 22:14.402
Why would she want to leave the island
and risk getting sick again?

22:16.738 --> 22:20.033
Then why do you stay with Jack?

22:20.075 --> 22:22.233
Because it was the right thing to do.

22:23.578 --> 22:27.332
Locke, he's a murderer.

22:30.710 --> 22:32.670
It's all about karma, Jin.

22:33.505 --> 22:35.215
You know karma?

22:37.092 --> 22:39.761
You make bad choices,
bad things happen.

22:39.803 --> 22:42.097
But you make good choices, good...

22:42.138 --> 22:44.516
Hey, hey! You got one!

22:44.557 --> 22:47.310
Here. Pull it in!

22:47.352 --> 22:52.180
Wow! Look at that!
You see? Now, that's karma.

22:54.692 --> 22:56.736
We must be the good guys.

23:11.459 --> 23:14.337
How long is that gonna go on for?

23:14.379 --> 23:16.923
Can't they fix whatever is causing it?

23:16.965 --> 23:19.207
That sound is not mechanical.

23:19.259 --> 23:22.554
You think somebody's doing that?

23:22.595 --> 23:26.015
- Somebody's banging on those pipes?
- Exactly what I think.

23:29.310 --> 23:32.272
Gentlemen, thanks for your patience.

23:33.773 --> 23:36.182
The captain would like to see you now.

23:52.417 --> 23:56.337
- Where's the helicopter?
- Lapidus is running an errand.

23:56.379 --> 23:58.923
- What kind of errand?
- I'm the doctor.

23:58.965 --> 24:01.801
- I don't know where he's going.
- To the island?

24:02.552 --> 24:06.504
- Know anywhere else he could land?
- What's he going to do?

24:06.556 --> 24:08.349
I said I'm just the doctor.

24:09.517 --> 24:13.730
- What did he say?
- He didn't say anything.

24:14.272 --> 24:15.940
What is he doing?

24:15.982 --> 24:18.026
Hey! Hey!

24:21.696 --> 24:23.782
That woman just jumped over the side!

24:24.866 --> 24:28.078
Don't just stand there!
What's the matter with you people?

24:28.119 --> 24:31.498
- What's wrong with you?
- Why aren't you doing anything?

24:31.539 --> 24:33.166
- Bring a rope!
- Get the rope!

24:33.208 --> 24:34.834
- Get a rope!
- Stop!

24:34.876 --> 24:38.713
- She just jumped!
- It's over. She's gone.

24:39.798 --> 24:42.123
Everybody get back to your posts.

24:45.095 --> 24:46.888
That was an order.

24:54.938 --> 24:57.649
I'm Captain Gault.

24:57.690 --> 25:00.235
I suppose you two have a few questions.

25:07.534 --> 25:10.662
- So, what can I do for you?
- What?

25:10.703 --> 25:13.665
- You wanted to speak with me.
- Start with why a woman

25:13.706 --> 25:16.167
jumped over the side
and you did nothing.

25:16.251 --> 25:19.462
I didn't jump in
or order my crew to jump in

25:19.504 --> 25:23.091
because I didn't want
to lose any more people.

25:23.133 --> 25:25.593
What exactly is going on here?

25:28.513 --> 25:31.891
Some of my crew
have been dealing with...

25:31.933 --> 25:36.104
...what might best be described
as a heightened case of cabin fever.

25:38.356 --> 25:41.526
It's got to do with
the close proximity of the island.

25:41.568 --> 25:44.143
- Why don't you turn around then?
- I've tried.

25:44.195 --> 25:48.491
But we have a saboteur on board. He's
done one hell of a job on my engines.

25:48.575 --> 25:51.119
I've got my crew working to repair them.

25:51.202 --> 25:55.832
- And then you'll take our people home?
- Then we move to safer waters.

25:55.874 --> 25:58.449
- My orders.
- I don't suppose you will tell us

25:58.501 --> 26:02.672
- who gave you those orders?
- Sure, I will. Charles Widmore.

26:05.383 --> 26:08.303
This is Charles Widmore's boat?

26:10.138 --> 26:12.015
That's right. You know him.

26:28.531 --> 26:31.201
Do either of you know what this is?

26:31.242 --> 26:34.662
It's a flight data recorder.
Otherwise known as a black box.

26:35.330 --> 26:38.083
That's exactly what it is.

26:38.124 --> 26:40.418
Now, here's the funny thing.

26:40.460 --> 26:44.714
This black box comes
from Oceanic flight 815.

26:48.301 --> 26:51.888
A salvage vessel recovered it
from the bottom of the ocean.

26:51.930 --> 26:56.841
It took a considerable amount of
Mr Widmore's resources to procure it.

26:56.893 --> 26:59.385
It was found
with the wreckage of the plane,

26:59.479 --> 27:02.148
along with all 324 dead passengers.

27:06.069 --> 27:09.239
Not the complete story,
as you are aware, Mr Jarrah,

27:09.280 --> 27:12.784
given the fact
that you are standing here. Breathing.

27:14.994 --> 27:17.622
The wreckage was obviously staged.

27:17.664 --> 27:20.875
Now, can you imagine
what kind of resources and manpower

27:20.917 --> 27:23.795
go into pulling off a feat
of that magnitude?

27:23.837 --> 27:26.297
Faking the recovery of a plane crash?

27:28.341 --> 27:33.012
Putting 324 families through
a grieving process based on a lie?

27:34.389 --> 27:36.516
But what's even more disturbing...

27:36.558 --> 27:42.105
Where exactly does one
come across 324 dead bodies?

27:43.982 --> 27:46.557
And that, Mr Jarrah, Mr Hume,

27:46.609 --> 27:50.822
is just one of the many reasons
we want Benjamin Linus.

28:03.084 --> 28:04.961
I'm sorry.

28:07.088 --> 28:10.175
I had to stop you any way I could.

28:13.178 --> 28:15.138
It wasn't your place to stop us.

28:15.972 --> 28:20.393
I know you don't trust me, but you need
to get off this island. We all do.

28:21.519 --> 28:25.221
- You want to leave?
- More than anything.

28:26.858 --> 28:30.862
I don't know if that boat out there
is the answer, but it's something.

28:33.323 --> 28:36.409
I need to go home, and so do you.

28:37.452 --> 28:38.620
Sun...

28:40.705 --> 28:45.126
In about three weeks, you'll be
in an almost constant state of nausea.

28:45.168 --> 28:49.923
A week after, you'll experience
shortness of breath that won't go away.

28:49.964 --> 28:54.719
A week after that, you'll lose
consciousness and slip into a coma.

28:55.553 --> 28:57.555
And then, Sun, you will die.

28:59.808 --> 29:03.426
And when your heart stops beating,

29:03.478 --> 29:05.271
so will the baby's.

29:07.899 --> 29:13.488
And that, Sun, is why it's my business.
Because you're my patient.

29:17.033 --> 29:18.868
If you go...

29:20.578 --> 29:22.455
...you will die.

29:24.707 --> 29:27.116
And your baby will never be born.

31:33.336 --> 31:35.828
So, what did you think of the captain?

31:35.880 --> 31:39.832
- He was surprisingly forthcoming.
- Yeah, he tells it like it is.

31:39.884 --> 31:43.054
Just don't piss him off,
know what I mean?

31:43.096 --> 31:47.267
I think you'll like your room.
It's on the quiet part of the ship.

31:47.308 --> 31:50.812
- The ship isn't moving.
- If you say so.

32:01.072 --> 32:03.533
That shouldn't still be there. Damn it.

32:07.078 --> 32:08.872
Hey, Johnson! Is that you?

32:10.498 --> 32:12.907
- Johnson!
- Yeah?

32:12.959 --> 32:15.003
Mop this up.

32:15.044 --> 32:19.549
- Sorry. I gotta go up on deck.
- No. You're gonna mop this up.

32:43.448 --> 32:47.118
- Kevin? This is...
- Sayid.

32:49.454 --> 32:52.290
- Desmond.
- Kevin Johnson.

32:55.627 --> 32:57.378
Nice to meet you, Kevin.

33:20.026 --> 33:22.185
I made dinner.

35:35.787 --> 35:40.375
Is the baby... mine?

38:46.978 --> 38:49.136
I can't believe you came all this way.

38:49.189 --> 38:52.108
Are you kidding?
Is anyone else coming?

38:52.609 --> 38:55.070
- No.
- Good.

38:56.696 --> 38:59.272
So where is she?

39:06.206 --> 39:09.292
- She's awesome.
- Thank you.

39:12.295 --> 39:15.006
Would you like to hold her?

39:15.090 --> 39:18.009
I don't know.
I kind of have two left hands.

39:18.093 --> 39:19.928
I trust you.

39:24.349 --> 39:25.767
Wow.

39:27.018 --> 39:28.978
She looks just like Jin.

39:30.897 --> 39:33.650
Yes. She does.

39:39.948 --> 39:44.160
So I guess we should,
like, go see him.

39:46.287 --> 39:47.956
Of course.
